# And it lasts as long as an n lasts, for the reason ss_val.up gives.
rule span_ph_T_dur takes 1 from ss_dur.obj
  bare
  call span_ph_n_dur
end

# And it lasts no time at all. The velar fricative is what a word-final r
# becomes here and it says nothing, so what its duration decides is only how
# long a segment with no amplitude in it stands between two words: Castilian
# gives the fricative something like ninety milliseconds, and any length at
# all is heard as a stop closure -- the b of amb, or a gap in the middle of
# carrer venir that casa venir has not got. ss_val.up says why the length
# went rather than the amplitude.
rule span_ph_j_dur takes 1 from ss_dur.obj
  call ZZfence_null
  set global half 2074 to 0
  match
end

# And the postalveolar lasts what a fricative lasts.
#
# Castilian declares S and never reaches it from its own spelling, so the
# number IBM left in span_ph_S_dur was never once spoken: 150, flat, for every
# S that does not stand after a t. Catalan reaches it constantly -- x, ix,
# caixa, xocolata, aixo -- and 150 is not a fricative, it is a held breath.
# Measured on our own output it came out at 145 milliseconds against 65 for
# the s of passa and massa, so the sound Catalan writes most often was more
# than twice the length of the one beside it.
#
# 80 is where it belongs: longer than the s, as a postalveolar is in every
# language that has both, and not double it. What is kept is the one context
# IBM did write, the S of an affricate -- tx of cotxe and despatx, which is a
# stop and this fricative and wants the short one, not a fricative of its own
# length after the stop has already been said.
#
# What is not kept is the scan loop that skipped synchronisation marks on the
# way left to find that t. It is three operations and a dispatch of IBM's, and
# the audio says it is not needed here: the t is found without it, and the
# fricative of cotxe measures 50 milliseconds and that of despatx 55. Neither
# number could be read until st_phone.up stopped laying down the phone C for
# tx, which nothing in the module speaks -- while it did, this arm was written
# and never once entered, because there was no S after a t anywhere in the
# language. The fricatives standing alone are 75 for caixa and peix and 85 for
# xocolata, down from 145 and 155, against the 65 of passa, which is
# untouched.
rule span_ph_S_dur takes 1 from ss_dur.obj
  call ZZfence_null
  plant test on_its_own
  call ZZlpta_load_vvg__setscan_0103l__4
  if answer is 0
    call ZZtest_string_s_4_1_ZZstring77                       # a t before it?
    if answer is 0
      set global half 2074 to 40
      match
    end
  end
  backtrack
place on_its_own
  set global half 2074 to 80
  match
end

# And the voiced postalveolar lasts what its voiceless pair lasts.
#
# IBM gave it 20, flat, in every context, which is a third of what it gives
# the voiced alveolar z and a quarter of what the fricative above gets. Like
# the S it was never once spoken from Castilian spelling, so the number cost
# Castilian nothing; Catalan reaches it from j, from g before e and i, and
# from the tg and tj of metge and platja, and 20 milliseconds of it is heard
# as a click rather than a sound. A listener put it exactly: the noise of the
# affricate is too quiet and too short, and it should be the sh with voice in
# it.
#
# So it is span_ph_S_dur's two numbers with the affricate's stop asked for
# instead of the fricative's. The voiceless affricate is t and S and the
# voiced one is d and Z, so the question is whether a d stands to the left --
# `cat_ph_d' in rules/constants, since IBM wrote a wrapper for the Z on the
# right and none for the d on the left. metge and platja take 40 and jove,
# gener and girafa take 80.
rule span_ph_Z_dur takes 1 from ss_dur.obj
  call ZZfence_null
  plant test on_its_own
  call ZZlpta_load_vvg__setscan_0103l__4
  if answer is 0
    call test_string_s 4 1 sym cat_ph_d                       # a d before it?
    if answer is 0
      set global half 2074 to 40
      match
    end
  end
  backtrack
place on_its_own
  set global half 2074 to 80
  match
end
